+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-2)** — plan for WP-BLD-D: shadow `badf-build` on every G07 self-dossier BADF has landed (`badf-build` → `SHADOWED`)\n\n## Stage-Gate\n- **Stage:** 5 workflow-integration → the controls replayed on the program's own builds, without affecting any gate.\n- **Decision:** Continue — rung D of the operator-authorized ladder (#188).\n- **Over-engineering risk:** a generator tool in the repo, or a shadow that claims coverage the corpus cannot give. Refused: the record is regenerated once from history and **recomputed by the tests on every run** (the badf-git precedent); every control with no historical corpus is declared as non-coverage, not implied.\n- **Glossary stage(s):** 7 build; no G08 term pulled in.\n\n## Observed (measured on `main` `6814a24` with the real tools — `ledger_landings`, `content_tree`, the artifact digests)\nThe corpus is **65 landed work packages carrying a G07 self-dossier** (WP-2026-0011 … 0098; WP-0010's dossier predates the ledger's identity window and is not on the ledger — a case class, not a gap hidden). On that corpus:\n- **request-digest-bound 65/65 `BOUND`** — every indexed evidence artifact recomputes its digest at the landed tree (a request never pointed at nothing, from WP-0011 on).\n- **authority-replayed 65/65 `AUTHORIZED_HUMAN`** — every landed WP's demand, as recorded on `main`, is `AUTHORIZED` by a human (C1 would have admitted every one).\n- **typed-binding-recomputed 1/1 `MATCH`** — the one BLD-B-era dossier's content tree recomputes from the object store (#196 adds a second).\n- **fresh-verification-replayed:** 55 `NOT_RUN_DEFERRED`, 9 `NOT_RUN_DEFERRED_WITH_RECORD`, 1 `PASS_WITH_RECORD` — history is honest about the pre-BLD-B producer: verification was deferred to compose, and where a unit-test `PASS` was claimed a composition record stood behind it (C5 replayed: 0 `PASS_WITHOUT_RECORD`).\n- **No historical corpus at all** for C3 (no WP declared `expected_surfaces`), C4 (no `test_obligations` on any landed WP), C6 (one ledger exists, no `RETRY`/`STOP`), C7 (no delegations). These are **non-coverage** of the shadow, to be declared verbatim and carried into the BLD-E admission.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0101 / BADF-DEM-0088)\n- `examples/build-shadow-evidence.json` generated from history under the corpus rule above with `measured_on` = the `main` that includes #196: case classes `request-digest-bound`, `authority-replayed`, `typed-binding-recomputed` (≥2), `fresh-verification-replayed`, `dossier-not-on-ledger`; counts as measured; `non_coverage` naming C3/C4/C6/C7 and the pre-ledger WP-0010; `runner_citations` for the #190/#193/#196 runs.\n- `tests/test_badf_build_shadow.py` recomputes every case from the object store with the real tools (digest recomputation at the landed tree, `content_tree`, the demand record) and **refuses a tampered record** (wrong digest verdict, wrong tree, a case that cannot be recomputed offline); thresholds at the measured counts.\n- `skills/badf-build/evidence/shadow-evidence.md` — honest first sentence, the measurement table, non-coverage named, why the root stays `VALIDATED` (admission is BLD-E, the operator's decision — pre-authorized on #188 but still evidence-gated).\n- Registry `badf-build` `VALIDATED → SHADOWED` (digest unchanged); doctrine section; DEM export; own composition record + typed self-dossier; reconciles the land-time-current WP. **No gate change, no schema change** (ladder-internal).\n\n## Tests\n- `test_shadow_record_is_well_formed_and_names_non_coverage` · `test_every_request_is_digest_bound_at_its_landing` · `test_every_authority_case_replays_from_the_demand_record` · `test_typed_bindings_recompute` · `test_fresh_verification_verdicts_replay` · `test_tampered_shadow_record_is_refused` · `test_doc_names_every_case_and_gap_and_root_is_shadowed`.\n\n**Version tier:** patch (evidence + docs + tests + registry status). **Lean mode:** advisory.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "recorded_at": "2026-08-30T16:40:32Z",
+  "provenance": "EXPORTED_FROM_SOURCE",
