+  "title": "GOV-0088: WP-VER-C — deterministic G08 controls in the canonical gate (exact target, one composed identity, independence/quorum, runtime credit, per-artifact non-coverage, blockers resolved, composed-result authority); badf-engineering-verification → VALIDATED",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-3)** — plan for WP-VER-C: deterministic G08 controls in the canonical gate (`badf-engineering-verification` → `VALIDATED`)\n\n## Stage-Gate\n- **Stage:** 4 prototype → 5 workflow-integration: the controls run on every G08 dossier the gate judges.\n- **Decision:** Continue — rung C of the ladder authorized on #195.\n- **Over-engineering risk:** a control that trusts a declaration instead of opening an artifact, a policy-epoch bump that strands WP-2026-0010's closed dossier, or a second validator. Refused (VER-I20): every control below is a `badf_gate.py` check on a typed G08 binding VER-B already validates, or on an optional Work Package field; controls fire only on fields that are declared, so every dossier on `main` stays valid.\n- **Glossary stage(s):** 8 engineering verification; G09 untouched.\n\n## Observed (measured on `main` `dcbcc54`, after #201)\nVER-B made typed G08 objects checkable **in isolation**: `check_g08_binding` refuses a bare-PASS review, an agent-produced observation, an unmapped contract result, a disagreeing transcript, a non-reproduced composition. Nothing yet judges them **against each other, the Work Package, or the composition record**: a review may bind one content tree and the observations another; a reviewer may be the dossier's author with no carried deviation; a C2 dossier may carry one ballot; an OPEN MAJOR finding may sit in the review while the dossier claims `PASS`; `composed-tree-test` may be declared `NOT_APPLICABLE`. Those are VER-I01/I04/I05/I11/I12/I15/I19 — frozen at A, producible since B, enforced at C. BLD-C (#196) proved the pattern: `check_g07_binding` binds `base_sha` to the WP's `base_revision` and `content_tree` to the composition record; VER-C mirrors it for G08.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0105 / BADF-DEM-0092 — re-measured at filing on `dcbcc54`; BARCHI-2 and BARCHI-1 both cleared) — seven controls, each failing-first and mutation-killed\n- **VER-C1 exact target (VER-I01):** every typed G08 binding's `target.source_revision` equals the dossier's `source_revision`; every `target.expected_content_tree` — and the composed binding's `composition.target_base_sha` — equals `work/<WP>/evidence/G07/composition-record.json`'s `expected_content_tree` / `target_base_sha` when the record exists (the BLD-C C2 lookup, reused).\n- **VER-C2 one composed identity (VER-I05):** all typed G08 objects on one dossier bind the same `expected_content_tree`; a review of tree X with observations of tree Y is refused naming both.\n- **VER-C3 independence and quorum by change class (VER-I04/I19):** a typed review whose `reviewer.reviewer_run_id` equals `independence.author_run_id`, or whose `reviewer.identity` is the dossier's canonical author, is refused **unless** the dossier carries an OPEN condition naming the independent-reviewer deviation (the single-collaborator condition: carried, never hidden). For C2/C3 the review's artifact **is** a verification record validated by `validate_verification_record`, with ≥2 (C2) / ≥3 (C3) ballots of distinct reviewers and runs, and `lenses_routed` ⊇ {correctness, quality/test} (C2) / + data/integration (C3) per `references/review-lenses.md`.\n- **VER-C4 runtime credit when demanded (VER-I08):** a Work Package may declare `verification_obligations: {runtime_required: true}` (new optional field, `work-package.schema.json`); when declared, every observation on a PASS dossier must carry a typed binding — a generic `agent`-produced observation is refused naming the obligation. Undeclared → silent (WP-2026-0010 unaffected).\n- **VER-C5 non-coverage per artifact (VER-I11):** a typed observation with empty `non_coverage` on a PASS dossier is refused unless the WP declares `verification_obligations.comprehensive_coverage_permitted_for` naming that type; the composed observation's own non-coverage (`test_set_epoch`) is the natural floor.\n- **VER-C6 review blockers resolved (VER-I12):** an OPEN MAJOR/CRITICAL finding in a typed review (or its verification record) refuses `PASS`; on `PASS_WITH_CONDITIONS` each such finding must map to a dossier condition whose statement carries the `finding_id` (the exit criterion \"review blockers resolved\", made deterministic); a review binding's findings ⊆ the record's findings ∪ withdrawn.\n- **VER-C7 composed-result authority (VER-I15):** `composed-tree-test` can never be declared `NOT_APPLICABLE` in `non_coverage` — a G08 dossier without a composed observation cannot pass; contract-test may (WP-2026-0010 stays valid).\n- All seven live in `badf_gate.py` as one **pure** function `check_g08_dossier(dossier, work_package, evidence, composition_record, record)` — no I/O, no git side-effects (deterministically testable; `validate_dossier` stays idempotent) — (unit-testable with in-memory objects + temp artifacts) wired into `validate_dossier` for `gate == \"G08\"` on PASS/PASS_WITH_CONDITIONS dossiers; typed in code, not walker-trusted (#171); no schema loosened; `lifecycle.json`, `badf_compose.py`, CI untouched.\n- Registry `badf-engineering-verification` `IMPLEMENTED → VALIDATED` (SKILL.md untouched); doctrine section; DEM export; own composition record + typed G07 self-dossier; reconciles the land-time-current WP.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_badf_verification_controls.py`, failing-first)\n- `test_c1_target_must_match_dossier_and_composition_record` · `test_c2_all_objects_bind_one_content_tree` · `test_c3_author_review_refused_unless_deviation_carried_and_quorum_by_class` · `test_c4_runtime_required_refuses_generic_agent_observation_only_when_declared` · `test_c5_empty_non_coverage_refused_unless_permitted` · `test_c6_open_blocking_finding_refuses_pass_and_must_map_to_a_condition` · `test_c7_composed_tree_test_cannot_be_not_applicable` · `test_controls_are_silent_when_fields_undeclared` (WP-2026-0010 end-to-end stays `APPROVED_WITH_CONDITIONS`). Mutation: each control's refusal disabled → its test red (7/7).\n- Existing `test_badf_verification_evidence`, `test_badf_g08_verification`, both contract tests, BLD-C controls stay green.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Shadow (VER-D) and admission (VER-E); any executor or ledger writer; changes to `check_g07_binding` / `self_dossier`; `badf-security-assurance`.\n\n**Version tier:** minor. **Lean mode:** **disabled** (independence / composed-result / fail-closed invariants — HARD INVARIANTS). **Shared surface** (`badf_gate.py`, `work-package.schema.json`) → objects-level QA + REV by a non-authoring seat before merge.\n\n🛑 **STOP — awaiting operator approval of this plan** (covered by the #195 A→E authorization; recorded here for the ledger). No branch, no files until VER-B (#201) has landed and the id triple is re-confirmed with the other seats.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
